          "slug": "news-publishing-platform",
          "reason": "The official README identifies superdesk/web-publisher as \"Superdesk Publisher - the next generation publishing platform for journalists and newsrooms\" and links the official manual. The manual documents persistent article records (article title, url, route, metadata, keywords, authors and media loaders) and an output-control gate: \"incoming\" articles \"are not yet visible online\" until \"assigned to a tenant, and route\", while the published list supports route changes, unpublishing and publishing to additional tenants; webhook events cover when an editor \"publishes/unpublishes/updates an article\", and original_url preserves the article's first URL after a slug or route change. Presentation surfaces are editorially curated and ordered: the manual says homepage teasers \"are curated by website editors using Content lists\", and in manual content lists editors \"drag and drop stories ... The order of articles here is the order in which they will appear on the front page\", with the order updated as news arrives. This covers the story record, gated/revisable publication and curated presentation layers. Scheduling/embargoes, a separately named correction workflow, newsroom planning/assignment and rundown are not claimed.",
